#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:39
msgid ""
"The level of access to a board is determined by a user’s assigned board "
"role. Individual board membership always gets precedence, followed by "
"highest (most permissive) group role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:41
msgid ""
"**Admin**: Can modify the board, its contents, and its permissions. By "
"default, board creators are also admins of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:42
msgid "**Editor**: Can modify the board and its contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:43
msgid "**Commenter**: Can add comments to cards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Viewer**: Can view the board and its contents but can't comment or edit"
" the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:47
msgid "System admin access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:49
msgid ""
"System admins can access any board across the server provided they have "
"the board's URL without having to request permission or be manually "
"added. When a system admin joins a board, their default role is admin. "
"System admins will have an **Admin** label assigned to their name on the "
"participants list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:52
msgid "Team admin access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:54
msgid ""
"Team admins can access any board within their team provided they have the"
" board's URL without having to request permission or be manually added. "
"When a system admin joins a board, their default role is admin. Team "
"admins will have a **Team admin** label assigned to their name on the "
"participants list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:57
msgid "Manage team access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:59
msgid ""
"Board admins can manage team access to their board by selecting **Share**"
" in the top-right corner of the board. On the dropdown next to **Everyone"
" at… Team** option, select a minimum board role for everyone on the team."
" You can also easily assign the new roles to the entire team and/or to "
"individual team members."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:61
msgid ""
"Minimum default board roles reduce permission ambiguity and prevent "
"security loopholes. The minimum default role means that board admins "
"can't assign individual board members a role lower than the team role. If"
" the team role is set to **Editor** then the board admin will only be "
"able to assign the **Editor** or **Admin** role to individual team "
"members. Lower roles will not be available for selection unless the admin"
" changes the minimum board role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:63
msgid ""
"Depending on the role selected, everyone on the team will have access to "
"the board with a minimum of the permissions from the role selected. Users"
" can get elevated permissions based on their individual board membership."
" The default team access for a newly created board is **None**, which "
"means nobody on the team has access to the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:66
msgid "Manage individual board membership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:68
msgid ""
"Only board admins can manage user permissions on a board, including "
"adding, changing, and removing members."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:70
msgid ""
"To add individual users from the team as explicit members of the board, "
"open the **Share** dialog on the board, search for individual team "
"members, then assign a role to set their permissions for the board. The "
"role for individual board members overrides any role specified for team "
"access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:72
msgid ""
"To change a board member’s role, open the **Share** dialog, select the "
"role dropdown next to the user’s name, then select another role from the "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:73
msgid ""
"To remove a member from a board, open the **Share** dialog, select the "
"role dropdown next to the user’s name, then select **Remove member**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:75
msgid ""
"Board admins can also add individual members using the autocomplete list "
"from @mentions and the person properties. To add an individual from the "
"autocomplete list, type their username in an @mention or in the "
"**Person** or **Multi-person** properties, then assign a role to the user"
" from the confirmation dialog, and select **Add to board**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:77
msgid ""
"On boards with team access, board members with **Editor** or "
"**Commenter** roles can also add individuals to the board from the "
"autocomplete list. Board members added in this manner will be assigned "
"the default minimum board role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:80
msgid "Channel role groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:82
msgid ""
"Board admins can add a channel to a board to grant all its members Editor"
" access. To do this, select **Share** in the top-right corner of the "
"board, search for the channel name, and add it to the board as a user. "
"The default role is Editor. Doing so also :ref:`links the board back to "
"the channel <end-user-guide/project-management/navigate-boards:link a "
"board to a channel>`, where the board will appear on the channel RHS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:84
msgid ""
"To unlink the channel from the board, open the **Share** dialog, select "
"the role dropdown next to the channel’s name, then select **Unlink**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:88
msgid ""
"A board can only be linked to one channel at a time. Linking another "
"channel to the same board will automatically remove the link from the "
"previous channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:91
msgid "Guest accounts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:93
msgid ""
"From Mattermost Boards v7.4, :ref:`guest accounts <administration-"
"guide/onboard/guest-accounts:guest accounts>` are supported in Boards. "
"Guests can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:95
msgid ""
"Access boards where they're added as an explicit member of the board. "
"`Team access <#manage-team-access>`__ and `channel role groups <#channel-"
"role-groups>`__ don't apply to guest accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:96
msgid ""
"Access existing boards, but not create new boards. Guests don't have "
"access to the template picker and can't duplicate an existing board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:97
msgid "Search for boards where they're currently an explicit member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:98
msgid ""
"Be assigned the Viewer, Commenter, or Editor roles, but not the board "
"Admin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:99
msgid "Only @mention current members on the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:101
msgid ""
"If you're not able to access this functionality, you may be on an earlier"
" version of Boards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:104
msgid "Share a board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:106
msgid ""
"Boards can be shared internally with your team or published externally "
"with limited accessibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:109
msgid "Share a board internally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:111
msgid ""
"To share a board with team members internally, select **Share** in the "
"top-right corner of the board, then select **Copy link** from the "
"**Share** tab below. Paste the copied link in a channel or direct message"
" to share the board with other team members. Only team members who have "
"permissions to the board will be able to open the board from the shared "
"link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:114
msgid "Share a board publicly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:116
msgid ""
"Sharing boards publicly is disabled by default. This means that the "
"**Publish** tab is not available from the **Share** dialog. To enable "
"public board sharing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:118
msgid "Go to **Product menu > System Console > Products > Boards**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:119
msgid "Set **Enable Publicly-Shared Boards** to **true**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:120
msgid "Select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:122
msgid "Once enabled, board admins can share a read-only link online with anyone:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:124
msgid "Select **Share** in the top-right corner of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:125
msgid "Toggle to the **Publish** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:126
msgid "Switch to the **Publish to the web** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:127
msgid "Select **Copy link**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:129
msgid ""
"Paste the link anywhere you want to share the board. Anyone with the link"
" will be able to view the board, but they won’t be able to edit the "
"board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:131
msgid ""
"Select the **Regenerate Token** icon in the URL box if you want to "
"invalidate all the previously shared links. Confirm the action to "
"regenerate the token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:134
msgid "Share cards on Channels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:136
msgid ""
"Cards can be linked and shared with team members directly on Mattermost "
"Channels. When you share a link to a card within Channels, the card "
"details are automatically displayed in a preview. This preview highlights"
" what the card is about at a glance without having to navigate to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:138
msgid "To share a card, you'll need to copy the card link first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:140
msgid ""
"Open a card and select the options menu **(...)** at the top right of the"
" card, then select **Copy link**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:141
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can open the board view and hover your mouse over any "
"card to access the options menu **(...)** for the card and select **Copy "
"link** from there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/share-and-collaborate.rst:143
msgid ""
"After you've copied the link, paste it into any channel or direct message"
" to share the card. A preview of the card will display within the channel"
" with a link back to the card on Boards."
msgstr ""

